RUN: mkdir -p %t.d
RUN: %PLC --constructors-only --relocatable --fpic %S/destructor_c_lib.pli -o %t.d/ctors.o
RUN: cc -shared -fPIC %S/destructor_c_lib.c %t.d/ctors.o -o %t.d/libchannel.so
RUN: %COMPILE -i %S/destructor_c_lib.pli %S/destructor_c_main.st -L%t.d -lchannel
RUN: env LD_LIBRARY_PATH=%STDLIBDIR:%t.d %t.out | %CHECK %s

Channel is a library FB: destructor_c_lib.c implements its body, FB_INIT and
FB_EXIT, and --constructors-only generates its constructor and destructor. The
program includes destructor_c_lib.pli and must call the library destructor for
its instances, not define its own.

CHECK: open 1
CHECK-NEXT: open 2
CHECK-NEXT: main done
CHECK-NEXT: close 2
CHECK-NEXT: close 1
CHECK-NOT: close
